      "description": "off or on. on: after each main-loop turn, pick candidate facts from the thinking, judge them with Haiku (one call per turn with candidates) and append the verdicts to ~/.local/state/dreeft/memory-shadow.jsonl. Never writes memory.",
      "default": "off"
    },
    "desktop": {
      "type": "string",
      "title": "Band on the desktop app (experimental)",
      "description": "off or on. on: also draw the band in the Claude Code desktop app. Untested: nobody has checked how the band draws there. off draws on the terminal only. VS Code and mobile never get the band.",
      "default": "off"
    },
    "steer": {
      "type": "string",
      "title": "Steering (experimental)",
      "description": "off, shadow or on. Changes what the model reads. When a turn has grown the context by 10 points of the window, and again at 20, a coin flip picks fire or hold. shadow: every trigger holds; each is appended to ~/.local/state/dreeft/steer.jsonl and nothing is sent. on: a fire also appends one hidden two-sentence note to the conversation, which the model reads, and a visible notice of it; both arms are logged. off sends and writes nothing.",
      "default": "off"
    }
  }
}

